  "sourceNotes": [
    "Source priority: the numbered five-page school handout defines required content; the 103-page enrichment slides support pictures and clarify clipped or mistaken text.",
    "Item 1: the labels ck, ght, gh, th, nch, tch, and ch are spelling patterns. Silent letters must not be sounded separately. The th words include both voiced and unvoiced sounds.",
    "Item 2: the full handout phrases are retained where slide extraction is incomplete, including a plate of rice, the new bag, beautiful girl, and many candies.",
    "Item 3: all 38 adjective sets are present. Ordering is grouped by the school slides rather than the scan column continuation; the words are unchanged.",
    "Item 4: prompts run from 131 through 209, producing answers 132 through 210. The four required examples are 136→137, 154→155, 198→199, and 209→210. Slide example 126→127 is outside the handout range and is excluded. Whether 210→211 is expected remains a teacher clarification.",
    "Item 5: the source defines cold-blooded as body temperature being the same as the environment. The child answer says body temperature changes with surrounding temperature, avoiding an absolute equivalence.",
    "Item 5: the source says a squid has ten arms. The child answer uses eight arms and two tentacles. The octopus answer stays eight arms.",
    "Item 5: tail regrowth applies to some lizards. The standalone chameleon prompt asks about color change without claiming camouflage is its only cause.",
    "Item 5: wasp labels are head, antenna, thorax, leg, wing, eye, mouth, abdomen (slide 59). Butterfly labels are head, eye, antenna, leg, thorax, wing, proboscis, abdomen (slide 60).",
    "Item 6 parent-only source note: the school handout lists China (including Taiwan and Hong Kong). The child list is Vietnam, Thailand, Malaysia, Brunei, Indonesia, China, Japan; supporting visuals should use neutral place labels.",
    "Item 7: school definitions are retained for assessment practice. Feedback should describe an action, never label the child lazy or bad. Obedience practice must not suggest following unsafe requests.",
    "Item 8: both Roman Catholic (Latin Our Father) and Non-Roman Catholic (Psalm 23:1–4) tracks are included. Parent selection controls which track the child sees; no belief is inferred.",
    "Item 8: the handout has the apparent typo I shall not be want. The reviewed image of enrichment slide 73 reads I shall not want; the app uses the slide wording.",
    "Item 8: Latin text follows the handout, with capitalization normalized. Psalm words follow slides 73–74 and are split into short learning lines. Neither prayer is truncated.",
    "Item 9: the school review options specify 46 Old Testament books for Roman Catholics and 39 for Non-Roman Catholics. Both tracks use 27 New Testament books. These are the school options, not a claim about every Christian tradition.",
    "Item 10: gross is retained as the handout spelling; German audio should pronounce it as groß. Übung retains the umlaut.",
    "Item 13: required animal spelling is paru-paro, as in the handout. Kalabaw appears only in enrichment slide 92 and is excluded from required progress.",
    "Item 14 is outside this app version, following the requested items 1–13."
  ]
}
